## Core Packages {.section-header}

The foundational packages for brain atlas visualization in R.

::: {.package-grid}


::: {.package-card}
![](https://github.com/ggseg/ggseg/raw/HEAD/logo.png){.pkg-logo}

### ggseg
[v1.6.8.9000]{.version} [OK]{.build-status .status-ok}

[Contains 'ggplot2' geom for plotting brain atlases using
simple features. The largest component of the package is the
data for the two built-in atlases. Mowinckel & Vidal-Piñeiro
(2020) <doi:10.1177/2515245920928009>.]{.description}

::: {.links}
[Docs](https://ggseg.github.io/ggseg/){target="_blank"} | [GitHub](https://github.com/ggseg/ggseg){target="_blank"}
:::
:::

::: {.package-card}
![](https://github.com/ggseg/ggseg3d/raw/HEAD/man/figures/logo.png){.pkg-logo}

### ggseg3d
[v1.6.3]{.version} [OK]{.build-status .status-ok}

[Mainly contains a plotting function ggseg3d(), and data of
two standard brain atlases (Desikan-Killiany and aseg). By far,
the largest bit of the package is the data for each of the
atlases. The functions and data enable users to plot
tri-surface mesh plots of brain atlases, and customise these by
projecting colours onto the brain segments based on values in
their own data sets. Functions are wrappers for 'plotly'.
Mowinckel & Vidal-Piñeiro (2020)
<doi:10.1177/2515245920928009>.]{.description}

::: {.links}
[Docs](https://ggseg.github.io/ggseg3d/){target="_blank"} | [GitHub](https://github.com/ggseg/ggseg3d/){target="_blank"}
:::
:::

:::

## Atlas Packages {.section-header}

Brain atlas datasets compatible with ggseg and ggseg3d. Each package provides polygon and/or mesh data for specific brain parcellations.

### Installation

Install any atlas package from R-universe:

```r
install.packages(
 "ggsegYeo2011",
 repos = c(
   "https://ggseg.r-universe.dev",
   "https://cloud.r-project.org"
  )
)
```

